 MFDS","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"p-Methylaminophenol Sulfate","CAS_Number":"55-55-0","EC_Number":"200-237-1","Chemical_Name":"4-(methylamino)phenol hemisulfate; Metol; 4-(methylamino)phenol sulfate (2:1)","Function":"Oxidative Hair Dye","Category_Code":"HD01","Category_Name":"Hair Dyes","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Restricted","EU_Annex":"Annex III (restricted)","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Restricted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Restricted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Restricted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"Yes","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"Specific concentration limit per Annex III entry; typically up to 0.68% in oxidative hair dye ready-to-use","Max_Concentration_India":"Not explicitly specified; aligned with BIS IS 4707","Max_Concentration_US":"No federal limit specified; CIR concluded safe as used in hair dye","Max_Concentration_Korea":"Restricted; MFDS safety standards apply","Format_Restriction":"Oxidative hair dye use; patch test recommended; label warning required","Baby_Restriction":"Yes","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Permanent hair color; also used in photographic developer applications","Key_Safety_Notes":"Methylaminophenol-class developing agent in oxidative hair color; contact allergen with potential for cross-reactivity in para-amino compound-sensitized individuals. CIR assessed as safe in hair dye use.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Data_Confidence":"Medium","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng Annex III; CIR safety assessment confirmed safe as used; CosmeticsInfo.org; EWG Skin Deep database","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng Annex III, India CR 2020, US FDA Hair Dyes guidance, Korea MFDS","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Ammonium Persulfate","CAS_Number":"7727-54-0","EC_Number":"231-786-5","Chemical_Name":"diammonium peroxodisulfate; ammonium peroxodisulfate","Function":"Hair Bleach / Oxidant","Category_Code":"HD01","Category_Name":"Hair Dyes","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"High","EU_Status":"Restricted","EU_Annex":"Annex III (restricted)","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Restricted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Restricted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Restricted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"Yes","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"Up to 60% in hair lighteners; EU requires mandatory label warning about occupational allergy and asthma risk","Max_Concentration_India":"Not explicitly specified; use governed by general safety provisions of CR 2020","Max_Concentration_US":"No federal concentration limit; FDA requires appropriate labeling","Max_Concentration_Korea":"Restricted; MFDS safety standards apply","Format_Restriction":"EU mandatory label warning: 'Can cause sensitization by skin contact and inhalation. Do not use if the scalp is irritated or the scalp or forehead has sores or damage'; not for use on damaged scalp; professional handling recommended","Baby_Restriction":"Yes","Pregnancy_Restriction":"Yes","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Hair bleach powder, hair lightener, highlighting powder","Key_Safety_Notes":"Strong oxidant and known occupational allergen; causes contact urticaria, allergic dermatitis, rhinitis, and occupational asthma - particularly in hairdressers (up to 18.7% sensitization incidence in multicenter studies). EU mandates specific warning language on labels. Both delayed and immediate hypersensitivity reactions documented.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"CIR Amended Safety Assessment of Persulfates (2017); Springer Nature respiratory toxicity systematic review (PMC9489562); DermNet NZ; Australian Industrial Chemicals assessment; EU Annex III mandatory warning text","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng Annex III, India CR 2020, US FDA Hair Dyes guidance, Korea MFDS, CIR 2017","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"1,2-Hexanediol","CAS_Number":"6920-22-5","EC_Number":"230-029-6","Chemical_Name":"1,2-Hexanediol","Function":"Humectant / Skin-Conditioning Agent / Solvent / Antimicrobial Booster","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None (CIR indicates safe up to 10%; industry typical 0.5-2%)","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None (no rinse-off vs leave-on EU restriction confirmed as of 2025)","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Toners, essences, serums, cleansers, moisturizers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Dual-function humectant and preservative booster; not listed in EU Annex II, III, or V; CosIng COSING REF 54170; CIR assessed safe up to 10%; mild skin feel","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng confirms no Annex restriction; CIR safety assessment confirms safe at cosmetic use levels; no rinse-off/leave-on split restriction as of June 2026","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng (COSING REF 54170), India CR 2020, US FDA, CIR","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"PPG-26-Buteth-26","CAS_Number":"9038-95-3","EC_Number":"","Chemical_Name":"Polypropylene glycol-26 butyl ether ethoxylated-26","Function":"Humectant / Emollient / Skin-Conditioning Agent / Emulsifier","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredi