regnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Moisturizers, serums, hair care products, cleansers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Ethoxylated glycerin derivative; free from restrictions; CosIng COSING REF 76277; mild skin feel and good moisture retention; no known irritation","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng confirmed permitted with no restrictions; CAS 31694-55-0 verified","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng (COSING REF 76277), India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"PCA","CAS_Number":"98-79-3","EC_Number":"202-700-3","Chemical_Name":"2-Pyrrolidone-5-carboxylic acid (L-pyroglutamic acid, free acid form)","Function":"Humectant / Skin-Conditioning Agent","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic (also natural: biosynthesized from glutamic acid)","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Serums, toners, moisturizers, hair care","Key_Safety_Notes":"Free acid form of NaPCA; most hygroscopic NMF amino acid; second-largest NMF component at ~12%; more acidic than sodium salt so may lower formulation pH; well tolerated","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"CAS 98-79-3 confirmed; CIR safety assessment for PCA and salts published; EU CosIng listed","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA, CIR","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Erythritol","CAS_Number":"149-32-6","EC_Number":"205-737-3","Chemical_Name":"Meso-erythritol (1,2,3,4-butanetetraol)","Function":"Humectant / Moisturizing Agent / Skin-Conditioning Agent","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural / Biotechnology (fermentation from glucose)","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Yes","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Moisturizers, serums, toners, sheet masks, lip balms","Key_Safety_Notes":"Sugar alcohol with excellent humectant properties; EU CosIng no penalty; also found in some fruits and fermented foods; non-cariogenic; excellent tolerance profile","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"CAS 149-32-6 confirmed; EU CosIng EINECS 205-737-3; GRAS food status; CosmeticOBS confirmed EU permitted","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Jojoba Esters","CAS_Number":"","EC_Number":"","Chemical_Name":"Complex mixture of esters from transesterification/interesterification of Simmondsia chinensis (jojoba) seed oil and/or hydrogenated jojoba oil","Function":"Emollient / Skin-Conditioning Agent / Moisturizing Agent / Texture Enhancer","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural (from jojoba plant Simmondsia chinensis)","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Yes","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Moisturizers, lip products, hair conditioners, solid formulations, sunscreens","Key_Safety_Notes":"Wax ester from jojoba; mimics skin sebum composition; primarily emollient barrier function rather than true hygroscopic humectancy; superior oxidative stability vs jojoba oil due to saturation; COSING REF 34778; well tolerated including by sensitive skin","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"No single CAS number due to complex mixture composition; COSING REF 34778 confirmed; available in various viscosity grades (15, 40, 60, 70); ISO 16128 natural origin","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng (COSING REF 34778), India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Ammonium Lactate","CAS_Number":"515-98-0","EC_Number":"208-214-8","Chemical_Name":"Ammonium (2S)-2-hydroxypropanoate","Function":"Humectant / Keratolytic / pH Regulator / Skin-Conditioning Agent","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted (Rx moisturizer formulations at 12% e.g. Lac-Hydrin)","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None (OTC cosmetic); Rx up to 12%","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Body lotions (especially dry/ichthyotic skin), moisturizing creams, keratolytic treatments","Key_Safety_Notes":"Ammonium salt of lactic acid; combined humectant and keratolytic action; used clinically at 12% (Lac-Hydrin) for dry skin/ichthyosis; cosmetic concentrations typically 2-5%; mild stinging on broken skin; EU CosIng COSING REF 74403","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"CAS 515-98-0; EINECS 208-214-8; COSING REF 74403 confirmed; FDA Rx drug use at 12% well documented; cosmetic use at lower concentrations widely permitted","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng (COSING REF 74403), India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Acetylated Hyaluronate","CAS_Number":"","EC_Number":"","Chemical_Name":"Acetylated sodium hyaluronate (partial O-acetylation of hyaluronic acid sodium salt)","Function":"Humectant / Skin-Conditioning Agent / Film Former","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Biotechnology (fermentation of Streptococcus zooepidemicus or Bacillus subtilis followed by chemical acetylation)","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Serums, moisturizers, eye creams, sheet masks, premium hydrating products","Key_Safety_Notes":"Acetyl groups enhance lipophilicity improving skin adhesion and prolonged retention vs standard sodium hyaluronate; more stable to enzymatic degradation; COSMILE Europe listed; no specific CAS as complex polymer; well tolerated","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"Medium","Verification_Notes":"INCI name confirmed via COSMILE Europe and INCIBeauty; no single CAS due to polymer variability; EU CosIng listed as permitted; emerging ingredient with growing clinical evidence for enhanced hydration longevity","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng (COSMILE Europe confirmed), India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Hydrolyzed Hyaluronic Acid","CAS_Number":"9004-61-9","EC_Number":"","Chemical_Name":"Low-molecular-weight hydrolysate of hyaluronic acid (enzymatic or acid hydrolysis; MW typically 10-50 kDa)","Function":"Humectant / Skin-Conditioning Agent","Category_Code":"HM01","Category_Name":"Humectants","Ingredient_Origin":"Biotechnology (enzymatic hydrolysis of fermentation-derived hyaluronic acid)","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Anti-aging serums, moisturizers, eye creams, sheet masks","Key_Safety_Notes":"Smaller molecular weight than native HA (10-50 kDa) allowing deeper skin penetration vs high-MW sodium hyaluronate; fragments can stimulate hyaluronic acid synthesis; EU CosIng COSING REF 59169; excellent tolerance profile","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"CAS 9004-61-9; COSING REF 59169 confirmed; distinct from sodium hyaluronate in MW range and penetration depth; clinical data supports improved hydration in deeper skin layers","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng (COSING REF 59169), India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Coco-Sulfate","CAS_Number":"97375-27-4","EC_Number":"306-483-0","Chemical_Name":"Sulfuric acid, mono-C8-18-alkyl esters, sodium salts","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"Not recommended for infants - irritation potential similar to SLS","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Shampoos, body washes, facial cleansers, toothpastes","Key_Safety_Notes":"Blend of C8-C18 alkyl sulfates derived from coconut oil. Marketed as SLS-free but contains C12 (lauryl) fraction; irritation potential comparable to SLS. Can cause scalp/skin irritation and dryness at high concentrations. Not equivalent to glucoside-based gentle surfactants despite marketing claims.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 97375-27-4 confirmed. Irritation profile studied by SCCS analogous to SLS.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Myreth Sulfate","CAS_Number":"25446-78-0","EC_Number":"246-985-0","Chemical_Name":"Sodium polyoxyethylene myristyl ether sulfate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Shampoos, body washes, facial cleansers, toothpastes","Key_Safety_Notes":"C14-based ethoxylated sulfate; milder and less irritating than SLES due to longer carbon chain and ethoxylation. Low potential for skin sensitization. Potential trace 1,4-dioxane from ethoxylation; must be controlled at manufacturing level. Generally well-tolerated.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 25446-78-0 confirmed. Low irritation substantiated in formulation studies.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Lauroyl Glycinate","CAS_Number":"2578-54-3","EC_Number":"219-919-5","Chemical_Name":"Sodium N-lauroylglycinate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Facial cleansers, gentle shampoos, body washes, sensitive skin products","Key_Safety_Notes":"Amino acid-derived (glycine) anionic surfactant. Very mild; low irritation and skin-compatible at physiological pH. Biodegradable and considered eco-friendly. Suitable for sensitive and dry skin types. Works well in combination with other mild surfactants.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 2578-54-3. Part of acyl amino acid surfactant class with strong safety data.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Potassium Cocoyl Glycinate","CAS_Number":"301341-58-2","EC_Number":"","Chemical_Name":"Potassium N-cocoyl glycinate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Facial cleansers, foam cleansers, sensitive skin body washes, baby products","Key_Safety_Notes":"Potassium salt of coconut-derived N-acyl glycinate. Mild amino acid surfactant with excellent skin compatibility; maintains skin barrier integrity. Works at slightly alkaline pH; common in foam pump dispensers. Biodegradable; well-tolerated across skin types including sensitive and acne-prone.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed. Acyl amino acid surfactant class; widely used in Japanese and Korean formulations.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Lauroyl Alaninate","CAS_Number":"13256-31-0","EC_Number":"236-267-2","Chemical_Name":"Sodium N-lauroyl-L-alaninate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Partial","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Luxury facial cleansers, sensitive skin cleansers, amino acid-based face washes","Key_Safety_Notes":"L-alanine amino acid-derived anionic surfactant. Skin-identical amino acid base provides excellent biocompatibility. Very mild; low irritation profile. Helps maintain skin's natural moisture. Premium ingredient common in Japanese skincare formulations. Biodegradable.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 13256-31-0. Alaninate-class surfactants have extensive Japanese safety data.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sucrose Cocoate","CAS_Number":"91031-88-8","EC_Number":"293-069-1","Chemical_Name":"Sucrose esters of coconut fatty acids","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Emulsifier","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Yes","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Natural cleansers, cleansing balms, cream cleansers, emulsifying cleansers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Sucrose ester of coconut fatty acids; food-grade origin. Very mild nonionic surfactant/emulsifier. Derived from sugar and coconut oil - both renewable. Skin-compatible; non-irritating. Functions as both surfactant and emollient. Suitable for sensitive skin and clean beauty formulations. Biodegradable.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; food-grade sucrose ester. GRAS-adjacent safety profile. Common in COSMOS-certified products.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Cocoyl Apple Amino Acids","CAS_Number":"","EC_Number":"","Chemical_Name":"Sodium salt of N-acyl (cocoyl) amino acids derived from apple protein hydrolysate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Yes","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"Yes - potential tree fruit allergen in apple-sensitive individuals","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Natural facial cleansers, amino acid cleansers, premium shampoos, clean beauty products","Key_Safety_Notes":"Novel plant-derived amino acid surfactant from apple protein hydrolysate acylated with coconut fatty acids. Very mild and skin-compatible. Marketed in natural/clean beauty segment. Theoretically low allergy risk but apple protein-derived component should be noted for tree fruit allergy sufferers. Limited long-term safety data vs established amino acid surfactants.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"Medium","Verification_Notes":"Relatively newer ingredient; EU CosIng listed under acyl amino acid surfactants. No specific CAS as it is a complex mixture. Apple protein allergy consideration noted.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Disodium Cocoamphodiacetate","CAS_Number":"68650-39-5","EC_Number":"272-043-5","Chemical_Name":"Disodium 2,2'-[(carboxymethyl)(2-cocoamidoethyl)imino]diacetate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Baby shampoos, sensitive cleansers, mild body washes, foam cleansers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Amphoteric betaine-type surfactant in the amphoacetate class. Very mild; excellent eye and skin compatibility. Effective at low pH (4.5-7); works synergistically with anionic surfactants to reduce irritation. Common secondary surfactant in mild formulations. Low sensitization potential.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 68650-39-5. Amphoteric class well-studied; SCCS no restrictions.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Cocamidopropyl Hydroxysultaine","CAS_Number":"68139-30-0","EC_Number":"268-761-3","Chemical_Name":"Cocamidopropyl hydroxy sultaine","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No - increasingly used in baby formulations as CAPB alternative","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Baby shampoos, sensitive skin cleansers, tear-free washes, mild shampoos","Key_Safety_Notes":"Amphoteric sultaine surfactant; milder than Cocamidopropyl Betaine (CAPB) with lower sensitization potential. The hydroxysultaine structure avoids the 3-(dimethylamino)propylamine (DMAPA) impurity issues associated with CAPB sensitivity. Increasingly preferred in baby and sensitive skin formulations. Good viscosity building and conditioning properties.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 68139-30-0. No SCCS restriction. Clinical data shows lower sensitization than CAPB.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Polyglyceryl-10 Laurate","CAS_Number":"34406-66-1","EC_Number":"252-011-7","Chemical_Name":"Decaglycerol monolaurate","Function":"Surfactant / Emulsifier / Cleansing Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"Yes","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Natural cleansers, micellar waters, oil cleansers, emulsifiers in creams and serums","Key_Safety_Notes":"Polyglyceryl ester derived from plant-based glycerin and lauric acid. Nonionic; very mild and skin-friendly. Functions as emulsifier and solubilizer. High HLB value makes it effective for oil-in-water emulsification and mild cleansing. Popular in natural/organic certified formulations. Biodegradable. Excellent safety profile.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; high ISO 16128 natural index. COSMOS/ECOCERT approved. Widely used in clean beauty.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Lauryl Betaine","CAS_Number":"683-10-3","EC_Number":"211-669-5","Chemical_Name":"N-dodecyl-N,N-dimethylglycine","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Facial cleansers, shampoos, body washes, foam cleansers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Simple amphoteric betaine surfactant without the amide linkage of CAPB. Mild, non-irritating, and compatible with all surfactant types. Better stability across pH ranges vs CAPB. No known sensitization concerns. Structurally simpler than cocamidopropyl betaine; considered mild and skin-compatible.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 683-10-3. Simple betaine structure; well-established safety record.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium C14-16 Olefin Sulfonate","CAS_Number":"68439-57-6","EC_Number":"270-407-8","Chemical_Name":"Sodium alkene sulfonate (C14-C16)","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"Not recommended for infant products","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Shampoos, body washes, liquid soaps, industrial cleaners","Key_Safety_Notes":"Anionic olefin sulfonate derived from alpha-olefin sulfonation. Higher irritation potential than sulfate-free alternatives; can cause scalp and skin dryness at high concentrations. Not typically used in sensitive skin or baby formulations. Effective secondary surfactant in shampoos. Mixed isomers (alkene and hydroxyalkane sulfonates).","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 68439-57-6. EWG and independent studies flag moderate skin irritation at higher concentrations.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Lauryl Sulfoacetate","CAS_Number":"1847-58-1","EC_Number":"217-431-7","Chemical_Name":"Sodium dodecyl sulfoacetate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Solid shampoo bars, facial cleansers, body bars, powder cleansers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Despite the 'lauryl sulfate' in the name, this is NOT SLS. The acetate ester linkage makes it significantly milder. Large molecular size limits skin penetration compared to SLS. Low irritation; suitable for sensitive skin. Very popular in solid bar formulations as SLS-free alternative. Distinct chemical structure from sodium lauryl sulfate.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 1847-58-1. Not to be confused with SLS (CAS 151-21-3). Distinctly milder class.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Magnesium Laureth Sulfate","CAS_Number":"62755-21-9","EC_Number":"263-796-4","Chemical_Name":"Magnesium polyoxyethylene lauryl ether sulfate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Low","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No - used in mild baby products","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Baby shampoos, sensitive skin cleansers, mild body washes","Key_Safety_Notes":"Magnesium salt of laureth sulfate; considered gentler than sodium SLES and particularly suitable for sensitive and baby skin. Lower irritation potential attributed to magnesium counterion. Potential trace 1,4-dioxane from ethoxylation (controlled at manufacturing). Used specifically where extra mildness is desired over standard SLES.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"No","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 62755-21-9. Used in Johnson's baby products historically; recognized as milder alternative to sodium SLES.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"TEA-Lauryl Sulfate","CAS_Number":"139-96-8","EC_Number":"205-388-7","Chemical_Name":"Triethanolamine dodecyl sulfate","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Foaming Agent","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"High","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"Yes","Natural_ISO16128":"No","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"Avoid combining with nitrosating agents","Baby_Restriction":"Not recommended for infant products","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Older shampoos, liquid soaps, industrial/professional cleansers","Key_Safety_Notes":"Triethanolamine (TEA) counterion raises significant concern: TEA can react with nitrosating agents (certain preservatives, contaminating nitrites) to form nitrosamines, which are potential carcinogens. EU regulations restrict TEA levels to control nitrosamine formation. Irritation profile similar to SLS. Considered an older formulation technology; largely being replaced by better alternatives in modern formulations. Not recommended in products where nitrosating agents may be present.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 139-96-8. Nitrosamine formation risk documented. EU Cosmetics Regulation limits TEA to 2.5% and requires no nitrosating agents in formulation.","Source_Reference":"EU CosIng, India CR 2020, US FDA, EU Cosmetics Regulation EC 1223/2009","Last_Updated":"2026-06-06"},{"INCI_Name":"Sodium Tallowate","CAS_Number":"8052-48-4","EC_Number":"232-491-4","Chemical_Name":"Sodium salt of tallow fatty acids","Function":"Surfactant / Cleansing Agent / Soap","Category_Code":"SU01","Category_Name":"Surfactants","Ingredient_Origin":"Natural/Synthetic","Concern_Level_TCS":"Medium","EU_Status":"Permitted","EU_Annex":"None","India_Status":"Permitted","US_FDA_Status":"Permitted","Korea_Status":"Permitted","Australia_TGA_Status":"Permitted","Canada_NHPID_Status":"Permitted","Vegan":"No","Natural_ISO16128":"Yes","SVHC_Flag":"No","CMR_Flag":"No","IARC_Group":"Not classified","Allergen_Flag":"No","Endocrine_Flag":"No","Max_Concentration_EU":"None","Max_Concentration_India":"None","Max_Concentration_US":"None","Max_Concentration_Korea":"None","Format_Restriction":"None","Baby_Restriction":"No","Pregnancy_Restriction":"No","IFRA_Restriction":"No","Common_Products":"Traditional bar soaps, laundry bars, household soaps","Key_Safety_Notes":"Traditional soap made by saponification of bovine tallow (rendered beef fat). NOT vegan or vegetarian. EU requires sourcing from non-BSE/TSE-affected bovine tissue - EU Regulation EC 1223/2009 Annex III covers animal tissue restrictions; tallow from specified risk material (SRM) tissue is banned. Consumers following halal, kosher, vegan, or vegetarian practices should avoid. Good cleansing efficacy but can leave residue in hard water. Being displaced by plant-derived alternatives.","TCS_Evaluator_Flag":"Yes","Data_Confidence":"High","Verification_Notes":"EU CosIng listed; CAS 8052-48-4. Non-vegan status confirmed. EU BSE/TS